puddle doctor (puddle 0.1.0, linux x86_64)

ok    CPU virtualization  on in firmware
FAIL  Hypervisor          /dev/kvm exists but you can't open it
      fix:  Add yourself to the group that owns /dev/kvm (usually kvm):
              sudo usermod -aG kvm "$USER"
            then log out and in again.
      from: /dev/kvm: Permission denied (os error 13)
ok    Bundled runtime     msb 0.7.7-puddle.2 (/opt/puddle/runtime/msb)
FAIL  Runtime starts      the file's permissions don't let you run msb
      fix:  Make it readable and executable again:
              chmod a+rx "/opt/puddle/runtime/msb"
            or reinstall Puddle.
      from: Permission denied (os error 13)
skip  Test boot           not checked: no usable hypervisor
ok    Disk space          120 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle)
ok    Disk encryption     data drive encrypted (BitLocker); swap /dev/dm-1 encrypted (BitLocker)
ok    SSH agent           the agent on /run/user/1000/agent.sock holds 1 key (ed25519: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)      version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store    a test write and delete worked

2 problems to fix before Puddle can run sandboxes. (1.2 s)

